\[
(x - y)^2 = (4z)^2 - 4(4z^2) = 16z^2 - 16z^2 = 0
\]
Thus, \( x - y = 0 \), meaning \( x = y \). Substituting back into \( x + y = 4z \), we get \( 2x = 4z \), so \( x = 2z \) and \( y = 2z \). Therefore, \( x - y = 0 \).

